%description:

Tcp.pmtudTimeout:rfc1191 -- the MSS of the handshake comes back 600s after the reduction.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Time after which the original MSS is restored to probe for increased path
MTU (RFC 1191, Section 6.3)".

The classes: rfc1191 (600 s, the default, the 10 minutes of RFC 1191 section 6.3) and other
(another value). The code: TcpConnection::sendSegment() restores the MSS of the handshake at
the first segment after the value has passed since the last reduction. This test separates "rfc1191" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, which sends to host2 through the router, whose link to host2 has an MTU
of 1000 bytes: 10000 bytes at 0.2 s, which reduce the MSS, and then 20000 bytes at 300 s and at
601 s. The restore comes at the first segment after the timeout; the burst of that segment keeps
the segment size that the sender computed before, and the next burst has the MSS of the
handshake, after the delayed ACK of host2 (200 ms). The test looks for 0.5 s at each part. Observation: level 1, the data of 300 s leave host1 in frames of at most 1000 bytes of IP; the
data of 601 s include a frame above 1000 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.pmtudTimeout
%# class: rfc1191
%# value: 600s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.pmtudTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPmtudTimeoutRfc1191")
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B && ipv4.totalLengthField <= 1000B")
             .describe("the first frame of data at the reduced MSS")
             .within(1.0))
        .act(action().at(299.95).describe("before the restore"))
        .never(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B && ipv4.totalLengthField > 1000B")
              .describe("a frame above 1000 bytes before the restore")
              .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(600.95).describe("after the restore"))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B && ipv4.totalLengthField > 1000B")
             .describe("a frame of the MSS of the handshake, after the restore")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPmtudTimeoutRfc1191 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.pmtudTimeout = 600s    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.router.eth[1].mac.mtu = 1000B
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 0B
*.host1.app[0].sendScript = "0.2 10000; 300 20000; 601 20000"
sim-time-limit = 602s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPmtudTimeoutRfc1191: PASS
